message_text:
feat(gitlab): provide support for gitlab based repositories. To enable the support the github based verification checks are refactord into own verificationConditions plugin. Also the plugin mechanism is tweeked a little so that the travis verification Conditions can now be optional.

The configuration for gitlab scenarios is as follows:
package.json
{
 "release": {
    "debug": false,
    "verifyConditions": "semantic-release/dist/lib/plugin-noop"
  },
  scripts: {
    "semantic-release": "semantic-release pre && npm publish"
  }
}

feat(gitlab): provide support for gitlab based repositories. To enable the support the github based verification checks are refactord into own verificationConditions plugin. Also the plugin mechanism is modified a little so that all plugins can be called with Array notation.

The configuration for gitlab scenarios is as follows:
package.json
{
 "release": {
    "debug": false,
    "verifyConditions": "semantic-release/dist/lib/plugin-noop"
  },
  scripts: {
    "semantic-release": "semantic-release pre && npm publish"
  }
}

docs: adds docker community plugin that supports major, minor tagging

@semantic-release-plus/docker is a fork of semantic-release-docker
converted to typescript and 100% test coverage added.

@semantic-release-plus/docker also adds the functionality to support
major, minor tagging.

